WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.380
- So I've had a lot of comments

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.327
on the channel over the years, being like,

00:00:03.327 --> 00:00:06.420
"Joey, you should share
your hair loss journey."

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.270
As if I have some epic tale,

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:11.910
a dramatic story arc,
infused with life lessons,

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.940
a coming of age tale, but in reality,

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.340
it's not something I've
really thought about much.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:18.400
Hair loss was always in the cards for me.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.970
Growing up, my dad really
didn't have much hair

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:22.900
and my two older brothers
shaved their head

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.020
due to male pattern baldness
when I was around 12 years old.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.450
When they did that at the time,

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.270
I didn't really think much of it,

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:30.957
probably for like five minutes, I said,

00:00:30.957 --> 00:00:31.890
"Oh, that's kind of weird.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:32.723
You look kind of dumb,"

00:00:32.723 --> 00:00:33.950
but then the novelty wore off

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.270
and they were just my brothers,

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:38.050
the same brothers that I
always knew since birth,

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:41.020
but when it was my turn and
I started seeing symptoms,

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.890
I wasn't so nonchalant about it.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:46.540
Growing up, I always looked
older than I actually was,

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.090
even right now that fact rings true.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:50.530
I'm 25 years old.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:52.420
A lot of people think I'm like 32.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:55.300
So when I was a kid, I
really took pride in the fact

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.720
that I looked older than I am,

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.490
that way I could boss other kids around

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:01.230
and seem like an adult
before I actually was,

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:02.950
even though I didn't have two brain cells

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.120
to rub together back then.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.717
So when I was 16 years
old, my barber told me,

00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:09.400
"Hey, you're starting to lose your hair."

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.030
I kind of freaked out internally.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:12.300
It's like the "SpongeBob" meme

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.487
where he's calm on the surface,

00:01:13.487 --> 00:01:15.520
but internally losing its shit

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.490
and I was like, "You know
what, this is kind of a bummer.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.160
Now I'm gonna look really old,

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.800
like I'm going to look 40 when I'm 17."

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.810
But I didn't really do anything about it.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.155
I started to notice that my hair

00:01:25.155 --> 00:01:27.540
was starting to recede at the temples,

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.270
but it was slow enough
that I didn't feel the need

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:31.490
to do anything about it.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:32.930
I was just hoping and praying

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:36.770
that my hair might last me
somewhat into university.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.180
Oh, we should probably just fast forward

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:41.300
to photos of me when I'm 18 years old.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.370
This is sort of high
school graduation territory

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.250
and you can start to see

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:48.424
that I'm receding at the
temples fairly significantly

00:01:48.424 --> 00:01:50.060
for an 18 year old.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:53.320
I definitely do not have like
a squared off head of hair

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.560
at 18 years old.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:55.400
And this is the summer

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.890
before I went into my
freshman year of university.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.238
So into university, you
can see that my hair,

00:02:00.238 --> 00:02:04.310
it's still there, you know,
it's still fairly thick on top,

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:07.060
but definitely lots
more temple is showing.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.070
If I had actually done something about it,

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:11.780
I would've had a decently
full head of hair to work with

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:14.500
and potentially experienced some regrowth

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.160
to the point where I would almost have

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.660
a full head of hair right now.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:20.220
You and me would be talking,
having this conversation,

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.500
actually, it's a one-way conversation,

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.820
I'm just talking at you,

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:24.400
but we would be doing this together

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.010
and I would have hair on the
top of my head, but I didn't.

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:27.890
I was in denial.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:30.000
I just said, "You know what,
I don't wanna worry about it.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.000
I don't really care that much."

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.390
But I think I did care.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:34.480
It did affect me.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.310
And we'll get into that
a little bit later.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:39.410
You can already see by
the end of my first year,

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.130
there's a lot of temple there

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.620
and I don't know what I was
doing with my hair at the time,

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.650
but it was not doing me any favors.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:48.660
I was slicking that right
back, kind of curling it back.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.260
You could tell, this
man is losing his hair,

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:53.790
like a middle-aged man at 18 years old.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:57.480
And I think at the time it
affected me subconsciously

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.650
whether I was aware of it or not.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:02.250
So I'd start to wear hats
a little bit more often,

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.690
trying to cover it up, but
the hair loss got worse.

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.950
Here's me at the start of my second year.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:08.290
There's a lot more forehead.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.760
I'm starting to keep
my hair shorter on top,

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.240
because I noticed it would just draw

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:15.480
a little bit less attention to the fact

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.620
that I was balding and I'd
keep my hair very short

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:19.290
on the sides as well.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:20.580
Just trying to do some techniques

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.940
that didn't look absolutely ridiculous.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.410
I didn't wanna look like I
was trying to hide the fact

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:26.790
that I had a receding hairline.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:30.360
I kind of wanted it just to
look clean and out of the way,

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.220
but then it got worse and obviously,

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:35.530
you know, that's what happens
with male pattern baldness.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:37.180
It doesn't just get better.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:40.733
So here's me playing piano
at some gig or something

00:03:40.733 --> 00:03:42.360
with my brother, Eli.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.370
I was cutting my own hair at that point,

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.640
buzzing it all the way up to the sides

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.910
and then leaving it lengthy on top.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:52.340
It kind of is an optical
illusion from the side.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:53.700
It makes me look like I'm kinda going

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:57.090
for that Mohawk look, but
it's not a great look.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.145
I do look very pointy.

00:03:58.145 --> 00:04:01.050
My entire head kind of
looks like a crescent moon.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:04.200
I think my third year is when
I should've bit the bullet

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.310
and shaved my head.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:07.870
I even started a YouTube
channel in my third year

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:11.060
and it was called, Better
Ideas and I had hair

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:14.300
and you guys can tell, it
doesn't look that great.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:17.950
It was starting to do that
weird androgenic alopecia thing,

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:20.210
where it was starting to
get thicker on the sides,

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.650
like right around the ears

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:24.210
and then kind of getting
a little bit puby on top.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.043
Sorry, mom.

00:04:25.043 --> 00:04:26.950
It just wasn't a very good look.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:28.350
It just didn't look fresh.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:31.190
It wasn't the best version
of what I could be doing

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:33.500
and here's the weird thing psychologically

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.880
as to why I didn't shave my head.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.730
It wasn't because I
wasn't aware of the fact

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.350
that I would probably look better

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:42.450
if I just bit the bullet
and shaved my head,

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:43.510
but it was just the fact

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.040
that I had lived my whole life with hair

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.770
and it was almost like I
didn't want to say goodbye.

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:52.340
I attached a part of
my identity to my hair.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:53.980
I almost felt like I wasn't ready

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:56.740
to become a new person by shaving my head.

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:58.970
I wasn't ready to present to the world

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.500
that I'm a new person now.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.140
I finally let it go.

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:03.530
I'm no longer in denial

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:06.410
and obviously you don't think
these things consciously,

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:10.020
it's just sort of a subconscious
identity crisis you have.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:11.650
You're kind of at a crossroads.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:15.380
Do I just let go of my hair
as a variable in my life

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:18.670
or do I continue to hold onto
it for whatever it's worth,

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:21.070
despite the fact that it's
not serving me anymore?

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:23.280
But I pressed on for
at least another year.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:27.310
This was when it really started
to just not look so good.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:30.070
I definitely have this sort
of like bowl shaped thing

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:32.410
going on on my head, two semi-circles

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.140
and from the top, it was starting to thin

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:34.980
right on the crown.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.310
So here's the year
before I shaved my head.

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:38.420
Everyone's looking suave.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:39.410
Here's all my brothers.

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:41.130
Here's a bald brother of mine.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:42.630
Here's another bald brother of mine

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:45.490
and then some non balds, look
at this non-bald right here,

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:47.690
non-bald right here, non-bald right here.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:49.130
Then here's the funny thing about Daniel,

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:51.570
is actually he was
starting to recede here,

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.560
but he actually did something about it

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:56.440
and now he has sort of,
you know, more hair,

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.750
like way more hair than he
did when he was losing it.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.450
That's what happens when you're proactive.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:03.190
So good on Daniel for not denying reality

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:04.470
so he can improve upon it.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:07.598
Either way, my hair's really
looking rough at this point.

00:06:07.598 --> 00:06:11.390
It's definitely like an
advanced Jude Law look

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:13.430
and I don't have Jude Law's face,

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:15.760
so it doesn't work as well
for me as it does for him.

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:17.350
So at the end of my fourth year,

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:19.820
the summer between fourth and fifth year,

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:22.610
I finally bit the bullet
and I shaved it off.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:24.520
All right, let's film this video.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:26.040
So I shaved my head.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:27.570
I think it looks a lot
better, to be honest.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:29.230
I was really postponing that.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:30.640
My hairline was like,

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.016
I mean, you can see where my hairline is

00:06:32.016 --> 00:06:34.370
and I had like a little
bit of hair kind of like,

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:36.660
that I'd do this with and
then you turn my head,

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:37.493
it'd be all thin up here.

00:06:37.493 --> 00:06:39.420
It looks like I'm not trying
to hide anything anyway.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:42.537
And I sent some photos to my
friends and family being like,

00:06:42.537 --> 00:06:43.840
"Yo, look, I shaved my head."

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.730
And they're like, "It looks good, dude."

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:48.150
That's it, you know,

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:49.980
I've met with some friends that summer

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:51.580
and they'd be like, "Oh,
you shaved your head."

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:53.460
I'm like, "Yeah," they're like,
"Yeah, it looks good, man."

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:55.980
That's it, you know, all that buildup for,

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:58.520
you know, 22 years or whatever it was,

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.847
led to the reaction of people being like,

00:07:01.847 --> 00:07:03.030
"Oh, it looks good."

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:05.740
And then treating me like
they've always treated me.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:08.090
You know, it doesn't really...

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:11.120
It's not a thing, like,
it just doesn't matter.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:14.120
And what I've learned
over this whole process

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:18.250
is that nobody cares, even
when my hair was receding,

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:19.880
unless you had somebody else

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:22.310
who was really self-conscious
about their hair,

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:24.217
they would probably compare
it with you and be like,

00:07:24.217 --> 00:07:25.675
"Oh, that guy's receding a
little bit more than me,"

00:07:25.675 --> 00:07:28.730
but all in all, you know,
nobody's thinking about your hair

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:29.690
more than you are.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:32.504
And when you shave it off,
it's not like a big reveal

00:07:32.504 --> 00:07:34.440
and it's like the "Princess Bride"

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.030
where you have this giant glow up,

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.390
there's a glow up in the "Princess Bride"?

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.470
No, "Princess Diaries", I think.

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:40.980
Yeah, it's not like that.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:44.050
Nobody cares, nobody cares
before you shave it off,

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:45.940
nobody cares after you shave it off.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.520
Your hair is just dead protein
on the top of your head,

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:50.010
do what's best for you.

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:53.100
In my opinion, if your
hairline is receding

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:56.100
to an advanced degree, it
probably will look better

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.110
when you shave it off,

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:59.480
but do I care if you shave
your hair off or not?

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:02.680
No, so just make the decision
based on what's best for you.

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:05.130
And funny enough, since shaving my head,

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:08.290
I feel like I have actually
gotten more confident,

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:10.330
especially when meeting strangers

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:12.590
and it's totally a subconscious thing,

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.510
because I don't have
to think about the fact

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:16.500
that I have an incomplete hairline.

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:18.050
I don't have a hairline anymore.

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:20.300
I literally can't have a bad hair day.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:23.600
I can also walk faster,
because I'm more aerodynamic.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.790
I can also tell when it's
raining quicker than anyone else.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:28.900
I can jump higher, swim faster,

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.650
I've basically become a
god, but in all seriousness,

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.920
the moral of the story,
I guess I can conclude

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:35.870
from my hair loss journey,

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:38.930
is that no one really thinks about you

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:42.860
nearly as much as you think
about yourself, not even close.

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:46.290
Most people, most of the time
are not thinking about you

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:49.000
and that might be a little
bit of a hit to the ego,

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:49.833
but it's the truth.

00:08:49.833 --> 00:08:52.340
Most people are mostly
thinking about themselves.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.740
So to think that people
are like sitting down

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:57.430
at a Christmas dinner,
thinking about Joey's hairline

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:59.840
is such a joke, but that's how our brain,

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:01.470
we always think that's gonna happen.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:04.070
The same could be said,
not just about hair loss,

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:08.140
but about a mole that you
happen to have on your upper lip

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:11.330
or a zit that you have
on your forehead one day.

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:14.010
It's a huge deal to you maybe,

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:17.610
but really you're just kind
of like a background character

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:19.200
in most people's lives

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.080
and they're not really
thinking about you at all.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:23.930
So why would you put
yourself through the trouble,

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:28.220
the mental distress,
to let that affect you?

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:31.950
So, yeah, that's the story
of my hair loss journey.

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:33.560
I hope you guys got something out of this

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:36.250
or at least just had some
fun getting to know me better

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:38.710
and you know, kind of picking apart

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:39.820
a little bit of my history.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:42.080
Maybe you could learn a
thing or two from this,

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:45.120
but if not, maybe you'll
learn a thing or two

